# https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/historical-national-statistics-notices-on-milk-utilisation-by-dairies-2023/usage-of-milk-by-dairies-in-the-united-kingdom-statistics-april-2023-published-01-june-2023
# In 2023, dairies consumed 1,239 million L of milk and produced 531 million L of liquid milk
# This leaves 708 million L of milk for producing processed products
# They output 44,400t of cheese, 19,300t of butter, and 7,700t of milk powder. (total 71,400t)
# Cheddar: 9.5 L/kg, butter: 2.04 L/kg, milk powder: 10.3 L/kg (average of 3 methods)
# Cheddar: 9.5 L/kg * 820kg / 385L = 20.2:1
# Butter: 2.04 * 820 / 385 = 4.34:1
# Milk powder: 10.3 * 820 / 385 = 21.9:1
# Average ratio given that mix: 16.09:1, or 100:6
# https://fromagestalbert.com/our-products/faq/?lang=en 
# The St. Albert cheese factory in Canada takes up ~12,500 m^2, and takes in 80,000L of milk per day.
# This means a 1x2 dairy takes in 160,000L of milk every 8 hours, or (160/8*6.4)=128,000L of milk every Simutrans month.
# This comes out to 332 churns(x5) of milk per month.
Obj=factory
name=Dairy1975
intro_year=1975
intro_month=12
copyright=James
level=2
population_and_visitor_demand_capacity=0
employment_capacity=36
mail_demand=10
class_proportion[0]=25
class_proportion[1]=25
class_proportion[2]=25
class_proportion[3]=15
class_proportion[4]=10
class_proportion_jobs[0]=20
